-- What the core 4th-level spells do, in a sentence or three of our own words. Shown
-- in place of the bare facts a spell's entry is built from (see Data/SpellSummaries.lua).
local _, ns = ...
local R = ns.Rules

R.SPELL_SUMMARIES = R.SPELL_SUMMARIES or {}
local S = R.SPELL_SUMMARIES

S["Arcane Eye"] = "An invisible floating eye appears within 30 feet for up to an hour. You see through it in every direction, with darkvision to 30 feet; a bonus action moves it 30 feet, through gaps as small as an inch."
S["Aura of Life"] = "For up to 10 minutes you and your allies within 30 feet of you resist necrotic damage and can't have your hit point maximum lowered. An ally at 0 hit points that starts its turn there regains 1."
S["Aura of Purity"] = "For up to 10 minutes you and your allies within 30 feet of you resist poison damage and have advantage on saves against being blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned or stunned."
S["Banishment"] = "A creature within 30 feet that fails a Charisma save is sent to a harmless pocket space, incapacitated, for up to a minute, then returns. An aberration, celestial, elemental, fey or fiend held for the full minute doesn't come back. One more target for each slot level above 4th."
S["Blight"] = "A creature within 30 feet takes 8d8 necrotic damage, half on a successful Constitution save. Plant creatures fail automatically, and an ordinary plant simply withers. 1d8 more for each slot level above 4th."
S["Charm Monster"] = "A creature within 30 feet that fails a Wisdom save is charmed and friendly to you for an hour, or until you or your allies harm it. It saves with advantage if you are fighting it, and knows afterwards what you did. One more target for each slot level above 4th."
S["Compulsion"] = "Creatures you choose within 30 feet that fail a Wisdom save are charmed for up to a minute. With a bonus action you name a direction, and each must spend its movement going that way on its next turn; it then saves again."
S["Confusion"] = "Creatures in a 10-foot sphere within 90 feet that fail a Wisdom save act at random for up to a minute: each turn a d10 decides whether they wander, do nothing, attack whoever is nearest or act freely. They save again at the end of each turn. 5 feet more radius for each slot level above 4th."
S["Conjure Minor Elementals"] = "Elemental spirits circle 15 feet around you for up to 10 minutes. Your attacks deal 2d8 extra acid, cold, fire or lightning damage to creatures there, and the ground is difficult terrain for your enemies. 1d8 more for each slot level above 4th."
S["Conjure Woodland Beings"] = "Nature spirits circle 10 feet around you for up to 10 minutes. A creature the aura reaches, or that enters it or ends its turn there, takes 5d8 force damage, half on a successful Wisdom save, once per turn. You can also disengage as a bonus action. 1d8 more for each slot level above 4th."
S["Control Water"] = "For up to 10 minutes you command the water in a cube up to 100 feet on a side within 300 feet: raise it in a flood, part it, change its flow, or make a whirlpool that drags creatures in for 2d8 bludgeoning damage unless they pass a Strength save. An action changes the effect."
S["Death Ward"] = "For 8 hours, the first time a creature you touch would drop to 0 hit points it drops to 1 instead, or the first effect that would kill it outright fails. Then the spell ends."
S["Dimension Door"] = "You teleport up to 500 feet to a place you can see, picture or describe by distance and direction, and can bring one willing creature from within 5 feet. Arriving inside something solid fails and deals 4d6 force damage to each of you."
S["Divination"] = "You ask a higher power one question about a goal or event within the next 7 days and get a truthful, perhaps cryptic, answer. Each further casting before a long rest has a growing chance of no answer."
S["Dominate Beast"] = "A beast within 60 feet that fails a Wisdom save is charmed for up to a minute and obeys your mental commands; an action gives you full control. It saves again whenever it takes damage. Higher slots last longer: 10 minutes at 5th, an hour at 6th, 8 hours at 7th."
S["Evard's Black Tentacles"] = "Tentacles fill a 20-foot square within 90 feet for up to a minute: difficult terrain. A creature there when it appears, or that enters or ends its turn there, takes 3d6 bludgeoning damage and is restrained unless it passes a Strength save. An action and an Athletics check against your spell save DC breaks free."
S["Fabricate"] = "Takes 10 minutes. You turn raw materials within 120 feet into a finished object of the same stuff, Large or smaller, or Medium if made of metal or stone. Fine work needs proficiency with the right tools."
S["Fire Shield"] = "Flames wrap you for 10 minutes. A warm shield gives resistance to cold, a chill shield resistance to fire, and a creature within 5 feet that hits you with a melee attack takes 2d8 fire or cold damage."
S["Fount of Moonlight"] = "For up to 10 minutes you glow, resist radiant damage, and deal 2d6 extra radiant damage with melee attacks. As a reaction when a creature within 60 feet damages you, it must pass a Constitution save or be blinded until the end of your next turn."
S["Freedom of Movement"] = "For an hour a willing creature you touch ignores difficult terrain, can't be slowed, paralyzed or restrained by magic, swims at its full speed, and slips out of grapples and bonds for 5 feet of movement. One more target for each slot level above 4th."
S["Giant Insect"] = "A giant centipede, spider or wasp appears within 60 feet and fights for you for up to 10 minutes, acting right after your turn on your spoken commands. A higher slot makes it stronger."
S["Grasping Vine"] = "Bonus action. A vine sprouts within 60 feet for up to a minute and makes a melee spell attack at a creature within 30 feet of it: 4d8 bludgeoning damage, pulled up to 30 feet towards it and grappled. A bonus action on later turns attacks again. It holds one more creature for each slot level above 4th."
S["Greater Invisibility"] = "A creature you touch is invisible for up to a minute, even while it attacks and casts spells."
S["Guardian of Faith"] = "A spectral guardian stands watch within 30 feet for 8 hours. An enemy that comes within 10 feet of it or starts its turn there takes 20 radiant damage, half on a successful Dexterity save. It vanishes after dealing 60 damage."
S["Hallucinatory Terrain"] = "Takes 10 minutes. Natural ground in a 150-foot cube within 300 feet looks, sounds and smells like another kind of terrain for 24 hours. Touch gives it away, and an Investigation check against your spell save DC sees through it."
S["Ice Storm"] = "Hail falls in a 20-foot radius within 300 feet: 2d10 bludgeoning and 4d6 cold damage, half on a successful Dexterity save. The ground is difficult terrain until the end of your next turn. 1d10 more bludgeoning for each slot level above 4th."
S["Leomund's Secret Chest"] = "You hide a chest and what it holds on the Ethereal Plane. An action with its tiny replica brings it to you or sends it back. After 60 days there is a growing chance the spell ends and the chest is lost."
S["Locate Creature"] = "For up to an hour you sense the direction to a creature you know, or to the nearest creature of a kind you have seen up close, within 1,000 feet. Lead blocks it, and a creature in another shape isn't found."
S["Mordenkainen's Faithful Hound"] = "An invisible phantom watchdog guards a spot within 30 feet for 8 hours. It barks when a creature comes within 30 feet without the password, and at the start of each of your turns it bites one enemy within 5 feet: 4d8 force damage unless the enemy passes a Dexterity save."
S["Mordenkainen's Private Sanctum"] = "Takes 10 minutes. For 24 hours a cube 5 to 100 feet on a side within 120 feet is secured in the ways you choose: no sound out, no sight in, no scrying, no teleporting or planar travel. 100 feet larger for each slot level above 4th."
S["Otiluke's Resilient Sphere"] = "A sphere of force encloses a Large or smaller creature or object within 30 feet for up to a minute; an unwilling creature avoids it with a Dexterity save. Nothing passes in or out and nothing inside can be harmed or do harm, though the creature can roll the sphere along."
S["Phantasmal Killer"] = "A creature within 120 feet sees its worst fear. It takes 4d10 psychic damage, half on a successful Wisdom save, which also ends the spell. If it fails it has disadvantage on attacks and checks for up to a minute, and saves at the end of each of its turns: damage again, or the spell ends. 1d10 more for each slot level above 4th."
S["Polymorph"] = "A creature within 60 feet that fails a Wisdom save becomes a beast of your choice, of a challenge rating up to its own or its level, for up to an hour. It keeps its hit points and gains the beast's as temporary hit points; the spell ends when those run out."
S["Staggering Smite"] = "Bonus action right after you hit with a melee weapon or unarmed strike: 4d6 extra psychic damage, and the target must pass a Wisdom save or be stunned until the end of your next turn. 1d6 more for each slot level above 4th."
S["Stone Shape"] = "You reshape a piece of stone you touch, up to 5 feet in any dimension, into whatever form you like: a weapon, a statue, a passage, a sealed door. No fine moving parts."
S["Stoneskin"] = "For up to an hour a willing creature you touch resists bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage."
S["Summon Aberration"] = "An aberrant spirit, a beholderkin, mind flayer or slaad, appears within 90 feet and fights for you for up to an hour, acting right after your turn on your spoken commands. A higher slot makes it stronger."
S["Summon Construct"] = "A construct spirit of clay, metal or stone appears within 90 feet and fights for you for up to an hour, acting right after your turn on your spoken commands. A higher slot makes it stronger."
S["Summon Elemental"] = "An elemental spirit of air, earth, fire or water appears within 90 feet and fights for you for up to an hour, acting right after your turn on your spoken commands. A higher slot makes it stronger."
S["Vitriolic Sphere"] = "Acid bursts in a 20-foot sphere within 150 feet. A creature that fails a Dexterity save takes 10d4 acid damage and 5d4 more at the end of its next turn; one that passes takes half of the first amount only. 2d4 more at first for each slot level above 4th."
S["Wall of Fire"] = "A wall of fire up to 60 feet long, or a ring 20 feet across, 20 feet high, burns within 120 feet for up to a minute. Creatures in it when it appears take 5d8 fire damage, half on a successful Dexterity save. After that, entering it or ending a turn in it or within 10 feet of the side you chose deals 5d8. 1d8 more for each slot level above 4th."
